---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'magnetic-field-strength-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Oersted to A/m converter — field strength H | maratool',
  description: 'Convert oersteds and amperes per meter — 1 Oe = 1000/4π A/m. Free browser magnetizing field converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert oersted to A/m (magnetic field strength)',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert oersteds and amperes per meter — 1 Oe = 1000/4π A/m. Free browser magnetizing field converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert oersted to A/m (magnetic field strength)', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert oersted to A/m (magnetic field strength)"
      lead="Type a field strength — read A/m, kA/m, or oersteds instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Magnet datasheets quote coercivity in oersteds (CGS) or kA/m (SI) depending on origin. The <a href="/magnetic-field-strength-converter">Magnetic Field Strength Converter</a> applies the exact 1000/4π bridge between them.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="magnetic-field-strength-converter" title="Try it — convert magnetic field strength units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Oersted (Oe)" to "Ampere per meter (A/m)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Magnetic field strength conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the ampere per meter (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many ampere per meters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Kiloampere per meter (kA/m)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ampere per meter (A/m)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ampere per centimeter (A/cm)</td><td>100</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kilooersted (kOe)</td><td>79,577.47154594767</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Oersted (Oe)</td><td>79.577471545948</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Millioersted (mOe)</td><td>0.079577471546</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>A ferrite magnet’s coercivity of ~3 kOe is 238.7 kA/m; NdFeB grades exceed 12 kOe (955 kA/m). If your two datasheets disagree by a factor near 79.6, one is in Oe and the other in A/m.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811" rel="noopener" target="_blank">NIST Special Publication 811</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/magnetic-field-strength-converter">Field Strength</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
